From c3f3b6b52f8cc8594d0e20fe919e4076ae69641f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:37:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0285 -- keep instrument-load wall-clock out of the FT
 accumulator

Patch 0280 excluded load_stage's wall-clock from the FIXED_TIMESTEP
accumulator during TAS. on_song_start() is the other main-loop blocking load
and was not covered: the GUS backend uploads .pat instruments to GF1 DRAM
there (file I/O + FPU). That time lands in the accumulator's next delta, and
the catch-up loop then runs up to MAX_CATCHUP extra tick_state() calls that
represent LOADING rather than gameplay.

Backlog beyond 5 ticks is already discarded, so each stall costs at most 5
spurious ticks -- but the campaign route triggers ~10 song starts, and ~50
spurious ticks is enough to consume the tail of a reel early.

Measured on g2k (v1.6.5 b421e5a52fea, POD-83 + PicoGUS, 9 cells): 4 of 9
clipped the reel's last two stage transitions, running 72/20/11/17/11/15/11/
19/11 instead of the full 72/20/11/17/11/15/11/19/11/14/11. Decisively, the
SAME configuration went either way run to run -- GC4 truncated while G31
completed, and OPL3.CFG and PGSB.CFG are byte-identical -- so this is
timing-dependent, not config-dependent. Cells that measured 9 stages of work
are not comparable with cells that measured 11.

Freeze/thaw excludes only the load interval, so unlike a per-frame clamp
(0281, defaulted off in 0284) it does NOT alter the logic-to-render ratio
during gameplay. Framerates stay representative, which is the entire point
of these replays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
index 3b04314d..37e5ffe3 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,11 @@
  * implementation: SMF parser + tick-driven scheduler. See
  * MidiScheduler.h for design + API contract. */
 
+#include "../tas.h"
+
+// patch 0285: FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator freeze/thaw (bodies in main.cpp).
+extern "C" void ft_accumulator_freeze(void);
+extern "C" void ft_accumulator_thaw(void);
 #include "MidiScheduler.h"
 
 #include "../Utils/Logger.h"
@@ -361,7 +366,30 @@ void MidiScheduler::start()
   }
   if (_backend)
   {
+    // DOS-PORT (patch 0285): keep instrument-load wall-clock out of the
+    // FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator during TAS, the same way patch 0280 does for
+    // load_stage.
+    //
+    // on_song_start() is main-loop context doing file I/O + FPU work -- the
+    // GUS backend uploads .pat instruments to GF1 DRAM here, which is slow.
+    // That time lands in the accumulator's next delta and the catch-up loop
+    // then runs up to MAX_CATCHUP extra tick_state() calls that represent
+    // LOADING, not gameplay. Backlog past 5 ticks is discarded, so each stall
+    // costs at most 5 spurious ticks -- but this route triggers ~10 song
+    // starts, and ~50 spurious ticks is enough to consume the tail of a reel
+    // early. Measured (v1.6.5, POD-83 + PicoGUS): 4 of 9 cells clipped the
+    // last two stage transitions, and the SAME config went either way run to
+    // run (GC4 truncated, G31 completed, byte-identical CFGs).
+    //
+    // Freeze/thaw excludes only the load interval, so unlike a per-frame
+    // clamp it does NOT change the logic-to-render ratio during actual
+    // gameplay -- framerates stay honest, which is the point of these runs.
+    const bool ft_guard = TAS::active();
+    if (ft_guard)
+      ft_accumulator_freeze();
     _backend->on_song_start();
+    if (ft_guard)
+      ft_accumulator_thaw();
   }
   // Arm playback now that the backend has finished any per-song setup (GUS
   // .pat uploads). cli/sti so the ISR sees the flip atomically vs the state
